From: djrobson5 <djrobson5@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:00:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] Metal: command list state, queue idle, occlusion query
 losses

Fixes found in a review of the Metal backend.

Quad clears: clearColor / clearDepthStencil with rects restored the
state cache after drawing, but the encoder held the clear's pipeline,
depth-stencil state, viewport, scissor, cull and fill mode and zero
depth bias, so the next draw with the same pipeline skipped setting
them and ran with the clear's. The cache now records what the encoder
holds (nothing for what the draw must set again). A stencil quad clear
also writes its value now: the clear states replace the stencil with the
reference value, which was never set to the clear's.

Queue idle: the present, acquire and wait command buffers plume commits
itself wait on the semaphores' events, and the present buffer's
completed handler uses the swap chain, but nothing waited for them.
Every command buffer of a MetalCommandQueue is counted until its
completed handler ran, and MetalCommandQueue::waitIdle (bounded) waits
for zero, for a resize and a shutdown to call before they destroy
semaphores or the swap chain.

setGraphicsRootDescriptor ignores (and reports once) an index the
pipeline layout does not have, instead of reading past the layout's
root descriptors (a layout without any, FABLE2_CONSTANT_BUFFERS off).
begin() clears the root descriptor tables of the list's last use.

Occlusion queries: a query that lost samples, because the pool has no
segment left or because it began inside another query, was read as 0
samples (occluded). It is marked, reported once, and getRawResults
returns METAL_QUERY_LOST for it until a reset. attachOcclusionPool lets
a list that continues a frame take over a pool's visibility result
buffer without a reset (which would wait for and zero the earlier lists'
counts), so its first beginQuery does not end the render encoder.

Shaders and pipelines: a library that did not compile (null) or a
function that did not build is no longer released or labelled.
